    {
      "@id": "docs/wireframes/fsh-guts/intent.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Observed (current checkout: main with #1010 `zrvt` merged)",
      "prov:value": "Page (`/fsh-guts/`), unchanged since the last draw, in reading order, inside the standard chrome. The chrome is the strip (mark, ☰, five icons, ⌂; the harness initials left it when #1022 folded the Harnesses group), the \"▾ Folio\" handle, search and footer.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1022"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/wireframes/fsh-guts/intent.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Findings",
      "prov:value": "Since #1010, every page also has a ⚙ **Settings** tile on the glass's bottom strip, larger and labelled. It does not hold the fish, and it does not point to the Settings that does. The bean's *\"under settings at dead fish icon\"* now matches one of two Settings.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/wireframes/fsh-guts/intent.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Findings",
      "prov:value": "## What PR #1010 (bean `zrvt`, merged) changed\n\n- **The fish did not move.** The ▦ Actions → Settings view, with the Discarded tile, is unchanged. That means screen 2's path is unchanged, and so is its count of 9.\n- **The glass gained its own ⚙ Settings** (theme, avatars, opacity, blur, tidy, defaults). It is a separate panel and holds no Discarded tile. It is drawn as screen 3, and it is the cause of the second half of finding 3.\n- **The fsh-guts tile gained the `glass` surface**, so the page is on the glass's bottom strip, on branches/ previews only (finding 6). This answers the owner's *\"where are the todo, fsh guts etc tiles on bottom of glass?\"* for the page, not for the viewer.\n- The `/fsh-guts/` page itself is generated and was not touched.\n\nAlso in this checkout, from #1022: the strip at rest lost its harness initials, because the Harnesses group now arrives folded. The chrome in screen 1 is redrawn to match.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean zrvt",
        "PR #1010",
        "#1022"
      ]
    }
  ]
